  "notes": "**Hutsix v2.3.0**(released)\n\n### Settings & Profiles\n- Fixed per-profile settings persistence: Auto Activate, Auto Pause On Focus Loss, and hotkey toggles now read/write the selected profile's JSON instead of a single global value, so each profile keeps its own settings across restarts.\n- Settings buttons now highlight when the selected profile has Auto Activate or Auto Pause On Focus Loss enabled.\n\n### Trigger Pass-Through\n- Added a per-binding \"Suppress trigger button while held\" option in the Profile Manager (default on). When off, the trigger button passes through to the target app while the action still fires, so a held trigger (e.g. RMB) can both cast its in-game skill and run the bound sequence.\n\n### Parallel Action Execution\n- Reworked the action executor: keyboard actions now run in parallel (bounded by `MAX_CONCURRENT_ACTIONS`), while mouse actions stay serialized on a single lane (one cursor). Actions that press the same key serialize via per-key locks, preventing double-fires and \"bind storming\" without any new profile flags.\n\n### Performance\n- Suspended the background screen-capture service while a side window is open, reducing UI lag when opening Settings / Profile Manager during an active profile.\n\n### Updates\n- The Update Available dialog now shows inline release notes when the manifest provides them (with a fallback link).\n- The download dialog now shows per-file progress, total size, transfer speed, and ETA.\n- After downloading, the app asks Install Now / Install Later instead of auto-launching the installer.\n- Update manifest (`latest.json`) now supports an inline `notes` field.",
